  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 348 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nAs the shortwave trough over the Great Lakes lifts off towards the \nnortheast, another trough over the Pacific Northwest will help place \nthe axis of the upper-level ridge over our forecast area. The \nperiphery of the upper-level ridge, seeing some deamplification from \nthe shortwaves passing to the north, will remain north of the \nforecast area, keeping PoPs low through the remainder of the week. \nBy the weekend, with greater southerly flow on the western edge of \nsurface high pressure, coupled with enhanced WAA from southwesterly \nflow aloft, heat and humidity look to rise enough to have heat \nindices break the triple digits south of the US-50 corridor. \nHowever, overall chances for this happening remain lower (15-20%), \nso future forecasts will have to monitor this trend to see if it \nmaintains.",
